        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Idrissa Ouédraogo, Jerry Paris\n- Roles: film director, actor, director\n- Places: Banfora, Upper Volta, Burkina Faso, Africa, United States\n- Topics: African film settings, rural versus city conflict, tradition versus modernity, television comedy\n\nFacts:\n- Idrissa Ouédraogo was born on 21 January 1954 in Banfora, Upper Volta.\n- Jerry Paris was born on July 25, 1925, and died on March 31, 1986.\n- Jerry Paris was an American actor and director best known for playing Jerry Helper, the dentist and next-door neighbor of Rob and Laura Petrie, on \"The Dick Van Dyke Show\".\n- Idrissa Ouédraogo is a film director from Burkina Faso who creates films set within Africa.\n- Idrissa Ouédraogo's films often explore the conflicts between rural and city life and between tradition and modernity.",
